# About Me — HTML Practice Page

This beginner-friendly page demonstrates:
- Valid HTML document structure (`doctype`, `html`, `head`, `title`, and `body`)
- Semantic elements including `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`, `figure`, `figcaption`, and `footer`
- A logical heading hierarchy (`h1`, `h2`, `h3`)
- An image with descriptive alternative text
- An unordered list
- Navigation links to page sections

## Submit on GitHub
1. Create a repository on GitHub.
2. Upload `index.html` and `README.md` to the repository root.
3. Open the repository and copy its URL for your assignment submission.

Replace the sample biography and interests with details you want to share before submitting.
